{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And all his brothers.</b> His relatives — the sons of Yishmael and Keturah." "<b>And to you.</b> With a kaf of the hey. (i.e., the suffix כה is spelled with kaf plus hey, plene spelling)" "<b>What then shall I do, my son.</b> That HaShem did not give Abraham anything but the land of Canaan, and I have given it all to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {2 "The phrase קרוביו is not in the biblical text; it is Chizkuni's own gloss identifying 'all his brothers.' The syntax of the second clause is elliptical, rendered hyper-literally; it appears to mean that since HaShem gave Abraham only the land of Canaan, and Isaac has already given it all to Jacob, nothing remains for Esau."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:22.427232337Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}